<h3>Step 2: Categorize and Handle Variance Items</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Exchange rate variance</strong>: Accept and record, process as forex gain/loss in the financial system</li>
<li><strong>Delayed rebates</strong>: Track rebate receipt timing, update the ledger</li>
<li><strong>Unreceived recharges</strong>: Contact agency or platform support, submit recharge receipts to follow up</li>
</ul>
<h3>Step 3: Set Up Recharge Alert Mechanisms</h3>
<p>Prevent campaign pauses from insufficient balance while reducing exchange rate losses from emergency recharges. Set a 20% balance warning threshold and arrange recharges 3 business days in advance.</p>
<h3>Step 4: Regular Reconciliation with Platforms/Agencies</h3>
<p>Don't wait until month-end to reconcile. Recommend pulling spend reports every Friday and completing invoice verification monthly to establish a consistent rhythm.</p>
<h2>Results: From $20K Variance to Zero Discrepancy</h2>
<p>Returning to Lao Zhou's case. After item-by-item investigation, the $20,000 variance broke down as:</p>
<ul>
<li>Agency rebate not received: $8,500</li>
<li>Meta invalid traffic retroactive deduction: $6,200</li>
<li>Exchange rate fluctuation loss: $2,100</li>
<li>1 unreceived recharge (agency processing): $3,200</li>
</ul>
<p>The amount actually requiring recovery was $11,700 (rebates + recharge), while exchange rate losses were absorbed by finance. After confirmation, Lao Zhou immediately initiated the recovery process and completed all collections by mid-December.</p>
<h2>Key Takeaway: Reconciliation Is About Financial Risk Reduction</h2>
<p>In overseas advertising, inconsistent recharge, spend, and invoice amounts aren't simple accounting puzzles—they involve multiple factors including platform rules, agency services, and exchange rate fluctuations. The core is establishing a mechanism of <strong>regular verification + categorized handling + proactive prevention</strong>, transforming financial risk from "discovered only at month-end" to "manageable daily."</p>
<p>If you're managing multiple advertising accounts with chaotic reconciliation processes and hard-to-trace variances, Yiyu Shumei offers multi-platform reconciliation support covering the full process from recharge verification and spend analysis to invoice matching and variance recovery.</p>
